# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and adjust. Vite only exposes VITE_* variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the dashboard sends API requests.
#
#   /api                      → same-origin; Vite (dev) and Vercel (prod) proxy
#                               it to the host configured in vite.config.ts /
#                               vercel.json. Avoids CORS entirely. DEFAULT.
#   http://localhost:8080/api → talk to a local backend directly, bypassing the
#                               proxy. Requires the backend to allow this origin
#                               in config/cors.php (port 5173 is NOT allowed by
#                               default — see docs/api/decisions.md Q9).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Running the backend locally
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no deployed API (docs/api/probe-results.md). The backend runs from
# the sibling checkout with Docker:
#
#   cd ../4th_year_projects_refractored
#   docker compose up -d                                 # nginx :8080, mysql, redis
#   docker compose exec app1 php artisan migrate --seed  # seeds the system_admin
#
# That serves http://localhost:8080/api, which is what vite.config.ts proxies to
# and what the Postman collection's {{base_url}} expects.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deploying to Vercel (Phase 15 — still no production host, by design)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is NOT a Vite env var — it is a Vercel *project* environment variable,
# read by vercel.json's rewrite (`$API_PROXY_TARGET`), not by the built app.
# Set it in the Vercel dashboard before the first production deploy:
#
#   API_PROXY_TARGET=https://<the real backend host>
#
# `vercel.json` used to hardcode this as `https://api.onwayride.me` — probed
# live and confirmed to be an unrelated Express service that 404s everything
# (docs/api/probe-results.md §1). There is still no known real production
# host, so the rewrite is now this placeholder instead of another guess.
#
# If this is left unset (or still wrong), the deployed app does NOT silently
# 404 every request one page at a time — `src/app/ApiConfigGuard.tsx` probes
# the public `GET /test` health route once on boot and shows a plain
# "No API configured for this deployment" screen instead of the dashboard.
